Organizations build custom applications like dashboards, admin panels, customer 360, IT automation, and service management tools to help their teams work more efficiently and effectively. Appsmith is an open-source low-code platform that streamlines custom application development, deployment, and maintenance.

## Installation

See the [Kubernetes installation guide](https://docs.appsmith.com/getting-started/setup/installation-guides/kubernetes)
for prerequisites, step-by-step setup, and platform-specific instructions (EKS, GKE, Minikube, etc.).

{{ template "chart.valuesSection" . }}

## External Secrets: per-key mapping

`externalSecrets.additionalSecrets` creates extra `ExternalSecret` resources. Each generated Secret is loaded into the pod via `envFrom`.
An entry's `secretStoreRef` is merged field by field over `externalSecrets.secretStoreRef`: a `name` or `kind` the entry leaves out is taken from the shared reference (then `secretstore` / `SecretStore`).
This example renames the AWS Secrets Manager keys `host`/`port`/`password` to the env vars Appsmith expects:

```yaml
redis:
  enabled: false   # use the remote Redis below instead of the bundled one
externalSecrets:
  additionalSecrets:
    - name: redis
      # secretStoreRef:            # optional, merged field by field over externalSecrets.secretStoreRef
      #   name: aws-secretstore
      #   kind: ClusterSecretStore
      data:
        - secretKey: APPSMITH_REDIS_HOST
          remoteRef:
            key: redis-prd-appsmith   # name of the secret in AWS Secrets Manager
            property: host            # JSON property within that secret
        - secretKey: APPSMITH_REDIS_PORT
          remoteRef:
            key: redis-prd-appsmith
            property: port
        - secretKey: APPSMITH_REDIS_PASSWORD
          remoteRef:
            key: redis-prd-appsmith
            property: password
```

## Testing

The chart ships with helm-unittest tests in `tests/`. See [tests/README.md](tests/README.md) for details on running them.

